From ec172531ec38fdd3ac2783d21e3faf6dc1e2b3f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:14:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: keep the glyph tracker count in bounds on a failed
 creation

The failed-glyph message handler ("The object resists the spell" /
"There is no clear floor") decremented track_glyph.num without a
check after writing through the current count.  When no glyph was
tracked, the count became -1, and the next commanded creation in
borg_defend_aux_glyph()/borg_flow_glyph() passed the count < size
guard and wrote before the start of the x/y arrays.  With the list
full, the same handler wrote past the end.  Only decrement when an
entry exists, and clear the tracked entry itself.
---
 src/borg/borg-messages.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-messages.c b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
index 09d1b883e..4f466f245 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-messages.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
@@ -1196,10 +1196,14 @@ static void borg_parse_aux(char *msg, int len)
     if (prefix(msg, "The object resists the spell")
         || prefix(msg, "There is no clear floor")) {
 
-        /* Forget the newly created-though-failed  glyph */
-        track_glyph.x[track_glyph.num] = 0;
-        track_glyph.y[track_glyph.num] = 0;
-        track_glyph.num--;
+        /* Forget the newly created-though-failed glyph.  Nothing was
+         * tracked if the list is already empty, and clearing the
+         * actually-tracked entry keeps the write inside the array. */
+        if (track_glyph.num > 0) {
+            track_glyph.num--;
+            track_glyph.x[track_glyph.num] = 0;
+            track_glyph.y[track_glyph.num] = 0;
+        }
 
         /* note it */
         borg_note("# Removing the Glyph under me, placing with broken door.");
-- 
2.53.0

